  "pdf_bytes": 731851,
  "selection": "Curated (audits of 2026-10-20). The first three prompts of the older fig:qual_main were viewed whole and at native pixels and all three were replaced; the medieval square that then took the middle row was replaced in turn (see 'replaced'). Eligible: the 195 evaluation prompts minus the four development prompts, the prompts of Figure 1 and every prompt displayed in another figure (galleries as displayed, showcase, ablation, failures, progressive). Rule: shortlist by SCA's ImageReward and MUSIQ_c percentiles within its own 195 images (eval/a4k195_main), keeping prompts where AReA and HRDiT each have ImageReward and HPSv2.1 at or above their own 25th percentile (asserted for every row; full attention is not constrained); view SCA whole and at native pixels and reject extra or repeated subjects, objects the prompt does not ask for, broken anatomy, seams, lattice or speckle; prefer varied subjects. The middle row was meant to show architecture or a street; every such candidate failed the viewing or the rule (see percentiles.rejected and percentiles.metric_stage), so it shows an interior still life, 2232973817337527860 (pink lilies in a vase by a paneled door). Its native pixels are clean; minor background quirks: a flat beige door with a brass knob and a wall plate beside the paneled door, and a squared back piece on the round table top; no subject is repeated. Clean at overview but not used, being a second landscape: 3638740675706761149. The rule constrains ImageReward and HPSv2.1 only; the baselines' MUSIQ_c percentiles are recorded in percentiles.shown. Ranking on SCA's metrics favours SCA in the printed values. None of the shown prompts is displayed in another figure.",
  "crop_rule": "Automatic, not hand-placed: fig_qual_main.auto_box over full, area, hrdit and sca, i.e. the 320x240 (width x height) window with the largest mean PIL FIND_EDGES response of the 8x box-downsampled greyscale images, at least 256 px from every border. The same window is cropped from every method; layouts differ between methods, so the crops differ in content.",
  "metric": "MUSIQ_c (CSV column musiq_crop1024): pyiqa MUSIQ averaged over four fixed random 1024^2 crops per image, crop positions set by the prompt id and shared across methods (Appendix app:metrics). It is a per-image score, not a score of the displayed window. Printed to one decimal; the best printed value per row is bold.",
